name: format-code
description: Format the project's code with Prettier before committing.
---

# Format code

Use this skill when the user asks to format, tidy up, or prettify their code.

## Steps

1. Check which files changed: `git diff --name-only`
2. Run the formatter on those files:

```bash
npx prettier --write "src/**/*.{ts,tsx}"
```

3. Show the user a short summary of what changed and ask before committing.

<!-- TODO: add an example for Python projects -->

## Notes

- Never format generated files in `dist/`.
- If Prettier is not installed, tell the user and suggest `npm install -D prettier`.
